      "title": "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "793f75bf-1c26-5de5-aff2-eb98d951161e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}(t)+2\\mathbf{h}(t))^{\\prime}$, where $t\\in\\mathbb R$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\langle 2,\\,2,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=\\langle - t,\\,- 2 t,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{h}(t)&=\\langle 2 t^{2},\\,t^{2},\\,0\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}(t)+2\\mathbf{h}(t))^{\\prime}=2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)+2\\mathbf{h}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 0,\\,0,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle -1,\\,-2,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{h}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 4 t,\\,2 t,\\,0\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 0,\\,0,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ 3\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle -3,\\,-6,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ 2\\mathbf{h}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 8 t,\\,4 t,\\,0\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}(t)+2\\mathbf{h}(t))^{\\prime}=\\langle 8 t - 3,\\,4 t - 6,\\,0\\rangle.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
